Nitro Control: License Scope
============================

This is a multi-license source workspace, not a relicensing of Linux, Arch
Linux packaging, Qt, PySide6, Python, NVIDIA software, or other dependencies.
File-level and upstream notices remain in force. See NOTICE.md for provenance.

New Original Project Work
-------------------------

The new, original Nitro Control userspace application and tests in
application/, project-original application launchers and service/policy
definitions, project-original build/verification helpers under scripts/,
project-original tests under the root tests/ directory, and project-original
operator documentation are licensed under the GNU General Public License,
version 3 or (at your option) any later version:
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later.

This grant covers original project material only. Already upstream-licensed,
copied, or derived material retains its applicable upstream/file-level terms,
even when located under scripts/ or tests/; it is not relicensed by this grant.

You may redistribute and/or modify this work under those terms. It is
distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A
PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt for the complete license.

Copyright remains with the respective contributors. No legal name, employer,
copyright assignment, upstream sign-off, or hardware test attestation is
inferred from an account name, machine path, or development assistance.

Kernel-Derived Work
-------------------

drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c carries GPL-2.0-or-later. Its local derived
16-line backport, packaging/0001-acer-wmi-anv15-51.patch, retains that license;
the userspace GPL-3.0-or-later grant does not replace it.

The complete Linux kernel retains its own COPYING, file-level licenses,
exceptions, and notices. The Arch-derived kernel PKGBUILD retains the package
license declaration GPL-2.0-only. See LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt and NOTICE.md.

Arch Packaging And External Dependencies
---------------------------------------

The vendored Arch recipe/configuration metadata is separately licensed 0BSD
by vendor/arch-linux-packaging/REUSE.toml. Preserve the Arch Linux Contributors
notice and the original maintainer attribution. The recipe's package license
field is not the license of the recipe itself. The full 0BSD terms with the
preserved Arch attribution are included in LICENSES/0BSD.txt.

Qt/PySide6 are dynamically imported dependencies under their own applicable
licenses. The separate Python userspace program communicates with Linux
through standard kernel interfaces; it is not linked into the kernel. This
workspace grants no new rights in external code, trademarks, or firmware.

Full license texts and their HTTPS provenance are indexed in
LICENSES/README.md. Retain applicable upstream licenses and provide the
required corresponding source when distributing covered binaries.
